# Build context for api/Dockerfile. Only requirements.txt and vault_api/ are
# COPYed; everything below is dev-only, state, or would leak local values into
# an image.
.venv/
# ** prefix required: a bare `__pycache__/` / `*.pyc` anchors at the CONTEXT
# ROOT only, so nested ones (vault_api/__pycache__, vault_api/routers/…) were
# still being COPYed into the image -- stale cpython-312 bytecode shipped
# alongside a 3.13 interpreter. Found in review.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.pytest_cache/
tests/
requirements-dev.txt
pytest.ini
README.md
cache/

# A real .env would put the operator's API key into the build context (and into
# any layer that COPYed it). The image takes its configuration from the
# environment at run time; deploy/.env is read by Compose, never baked in.
.env
